<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">N'Djamena</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fort-Lamy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">N'Djamena is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, at the confluence of the Chari and Logone rivers on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>. It was founded by the French in 1900 as Fort-Lamy, named after the officer François Lamy, who was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kousseri">Battle of Kousséri</a> that year, and was the capital of the colony of Chad. It was renamed N'Djamena in 1973.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ndjamena.jpg" alt="N'Djamena" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kayhan ERTUGRUL · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Building_of_National_Assembly_DJAMENA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
